 abstract = {This chapter discusses securing shared cloud computing. Cloud computing is changing the concept of network boundaries. The chapter looks at both the advantages and disadvantages of virtualization and cloud computing as well as the concerns that they raise for enterprise security. It also discusses compliance frameworks and legal considerations that can impact organization, such as contract and agreement types. These topics are the items that CompTIA expects a security practitioner to know for the exam. Data consideration, third&#x2010;party attestation, regulations, and standards are all very important to compliance and vendor risk. Many substantial security risks arise when merging enterprises or hiring third&#x2010;party organizations. These risks may be the result of a vendor relationship that starts somewhere along the organization's supply chain, or they may be the result of other business partnerships or conflicts within the merged entity.},
